e some.\n\n**Mode 4 (`static` with a specific count)**: This mode lets you specify an explicit number of CCS engines to create.\n\n## When to Use Mode 4\n\nYou'd use mode 4 when you want **explicit control over the number of CCS instances** \u2014 for example, when benchmarking or tuning performance for a specific workload. If you have a compute-heavy workload (like machine learning inference, scientific computing, or large OpenCL kernels) that saturates a single CCS, you can pin the number of engines to match your needs.\n\n---\n\n**A note of honesty:** The exact numeric semantics of these modes (especially the distinction between the \"static\" variants and whether mode 4 takes a"}